Now that your .gitignore file has the rules, go back to your terminal (which is still at C:\...ClaimConnect>) and run these commands again, one by one.

This time, you will not see any warnings.

Add all the files (the correct way):

Bash

git add .

Create your "save point":

Bash

git commit -m "Initial commit: All backend services working without security"

Set your main branch name:

Bash

git branch -M main

Link your local folder to GitHub:

Bash

git remote add origin https://github.com/srikardasireddi/ClaimConnect-Microservices.git

Push (Upload) your code:

Bash

git push -u origin main

After this, your code will be on GitHub. Then you can run the final two commands to create your safe "security" branch:

Bash

git checkout -b feat/security
git push -u origin feat/security